></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6893-drazhya","user":"Drazhya","date":". 03-26-2019, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6893-drazhya","name":"Drazhya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T22:31:46-07:00","id":1300197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1300090#post1300090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you treating quilin as mundane animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I would use that Chimera charm to mix a lion with some kind of deer that has scales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T01:31:04-07:00","id":1300216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1300197#post1300197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, I would use that Chimera charm to mix a lion with some kind of deer that has scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Extra Limb -&gt; Centaur and Unusual Hide 4 or 5?<br /> <br /> Edit: If you are going Centaur, you don\u2019t even need Lion! Just Deer + Fish or something. Where the lion head should be is your torso.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:24:20-07:00","id":1300239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1300216#post1300216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... Extra Limb -&gt; Centaur and Unusual Hide 4 or 5?<br /> <br /> Edit: If you are going Centaur, you don\u2019t even need Lion! Just Deer + Fish or something. Where the lion head should be is your torso.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sketching him atm and a lion's paws looks better than hooves for me.<br /> <br /> Though I can make that the antler and scales come from an artirfact mask and armor, so he'll only need lion as a spirit shape now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-27-2019, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:24:58-07:00","id":1300240,"title":"","content":"The idea of combining a lion with a horned, hoofed mammal, and then making a centaur out of it, kinda reminds me of Legend of Zelda's Lynels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:29:10-07:00","id":1300242,"title":"","content":"Presumably the idea is that the spirit shape is some kind of qilin as well, so you need the lion in the mix. The scales could be a mutation the character already has that just carried over to their spirit shape though. Then you just need the two animals. Or if you don't mind what hoofed animal forms the main body, there's simhata for hoof-beast and lion head + fish for scales and carp whiskers. Doesn't get you antlers or horns though. Heck, you probably had the best idea from the start, the setting has scaled jaguars, there's probably scaled deer bouncing gracefully around somewhere if your ST allows it. Damn, now I'm thinking of carp-deer and they're oddly cute.<br /> <br /> I hope your qilin-centaur works out, however you do it. And I hope we get art because it sounds amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:31:26-07:00","id":1300243,"title":"","content":"You could maybe do it as a lion-deer thing mixed with a fish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T17:34:26-07:00","id":1300426,"title":"","content":"I'm contemplating making a swordsman/duelist who enjoys hunting fae a little too much, with a beetle totem. He'd try to gather promising individuals and make a wandering swordsman dojo, or 'hunter's guild'. Hollow Knight meets Goblin Slayer meets Holy Blade Ludwig from Bloodborne.<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=601\" data-tempid=\"temp_601_1553732903773_705\" /><br /> But mostly played for laughs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 03-27-2019, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:06:01-07:00","id":1300583,"title":"","content":"While I've not seen it used in a game, steel devil style looks to my eye, (and from a few comments here) like an art that lets you crush opponents who you were going to defeat anyway. It has no tools to handle strong parries and dodges. But a lunar using it could mix in stuff like finding the needle's eye and striking mospid method. That looks like fun to me.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a good choice changing moon general trying to win an empire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T16:04:50-07:00","id":1300697,"title":"","content":"A wicked old sorcerer who, reliving the moment that sent him down his dark path, finally did the right thing. Exalted, he has been returned to boyhood through something like the Blessed Transformation, and now he's out to <i>earn</i> this second chance while trying to be rid of the man he was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T18:19:59-07:00","id":1300719,"title":"","content":"Carmen Sandiego--A lunar who was a daughter of a patrician who exalted after her family was driven into Penury. Now, she steels both material and immaterial things from the Realm, stricking them right in their dignity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T02:14:09-07:00","id":1300782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1300719#post1300719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carmen Sandiego--A lunar who was a daughter of a patrician who exalted after her family was driven into Penury. Now, she steels both material and immaterial things from the Realm, stricking them right in their dignity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where in the world can I find her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T18:23:25-07:00","id":1300992,"title":"","content":"Well when we have the rules for necromancy I plan on making Scours the Battlefield. <br /> Scours is a necromatic prodigy that travels battlefields laying ghosts to rest and uses the underworld to avoid/escape the Wyld Hunt. <br /> I haven't decided if Scours has a Solar mate that is horrified by anyone associated with the dead or an Abyssal that is horrified that anyone would dare lay ghosts to rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T03:43:56-07:00","id":1301051,"title":"","content":"I had an dea once for a horse totem Lunar. a former cavalryman, he can now be both the rider or the mount.<br /> <br /> it fell through when my sick mind couldn't not give him a big horsecock for a tell :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T13:30:41-07:00","id":1301136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1299878#post1299878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of reminded of the whole business with police conveniently not having their body cams turned on, not tracking how many people they kill, being encouraged by their own chiefs to erase bad marks off their records, and so on; sure, not every cop is bad, but the system <i>as a whole...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I would go so far as to say that most cops are great, but the system itself may have serious inherent flaws, and in some places the force is hopelessly corrupt because of hopelessly corrupt local government making it impossible for an honest cop to hold power within the rigged system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T16:03:33-07:00","id":1301176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1301136#post1301136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go so far as to say that most cops are great, but the system itself may have serious inherent flaws, and in some places the force is hopelessly corrupt because of hopelessly corrupt local government making it impossible for an honest cop to hold power within the rigged system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would certainly be the narrative preferred by film and television as it\u2019s much simpler to label the problem as criminal corruption than \u201cthe foundation these laws and policies are built on was intentionally designed to facilitate racial oppression, and we haven\u2019t been willing to pull them up by the root\u201d as tha doesn\u2019t provide conveniently identifiable beatable villains.<br /> <br /> I mean just look at *gestures at entirety of the \u201cwar on drugs\u201d and prison-industrial complex*<br /> <br /> If it was a problem of a few corrupt local governments the US wouldn\u2019t so vastly outstrip every other nation on Earth on incarcerating our own citizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-30-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T21:58:06-07:00","id":1301227,"title":"","content":"I watched the Met Opera <i>Die Walk\u00fcre</i> this morning and now I really want to do a Wotan expy as a No Moon: the aggressively transgressive witch-king. It's less the Raksi &quot;doing it to fuck with you&quot;, and more &quot;doing it because he wants to see what can be accomplished&quot;. Conducting social experiments in weaponizing societies through generational shenanigans.<br /> <br /> If I run a Lunars game, he will absolutely be appearing as a shahan-ya.<br /> <br /> (Also, Act II is a wonderful example of what happens when you have too many Defining Intimacies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T02:29:10-07:00","id":1301255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1301176#post1301176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would certainly be the narrative preferred by film and television as it\u2019s much simpler to label the problem as criminal corruption than \u201cthe foundation these laws and policies are built on was intentionally designed to facilitate racial oppression, and we haven\u2019t been willing to pull them up by the root\u201d as tha doesn\u2019t provide conveniently identifiable beatable villains.<br /> <br /> I mean just look at *gestures at entirety of the \u201cwar on drugs\u201d and prison-industrial complex*<br /> <br /> If it was a problem of a few corrupt local governments the US wouldn\u2019t so vastly outstrip every other nation on Earth on incarcerating our own citizens.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes you feel any better... you also massively outstrip other developed countries on police shootings! American police shoot more people dead a year than have been shot dead by police in England and Wales since 1945.<br /> <br /> Though I will say that a terrible system doesn't mean most cops are evil, so much as they're stuck in a terrible system that trains them to respond in certain ways. I think a big factor is America's enormous gun murder rate, which makes US cops worry a lot about being shot in a way that our police don't. I mean, being a policeman in the USA is more dangerous than being a policeman in Northern Ireland, where there are actual terrorist groups who deliberately target policemen. Outside NI, most of our police don't carry guns, so even if they are racist or paranoid they can't shoot people dead, but then our criminals and terrorists don't normally have guns either. The US law enforcement environment is so high-stress, high-danger, racially-charged, that it pushes cops to behave with excessive force, or, they worry, die.<br /> <br /> I read about a US cop a couple of years ago who was fired for not shooting an unarmed black man. With that kind of thing, it's no wonder that the cops end upl bad.llll<br /> <br /> Incidentally... How did this conversation start, and what's the relevance to Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:03:50-07:00","id":1301286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1299878#post1299878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of reminded of the whole business with police conveniently not having their body cams turned on, not tracking how many people they kill, being encouraged by their own chiefs to erase bad marks off their records, and so on; sure, not every cop is bad, but the system <i>as a whole...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is the post that started the detour into the inherit injustice of the US justice system. While race factors heavily in the equation, so does wealth.<br /> <br /> So new concept, trying into the debate.<br /> <br /> Grabbed by the garrison forces of a realm satrapy and forced into slavery for a crime he didn't commit the character is exalted and escaped and becomes after training from the Silver Pact a revolutionary leader in the satrapy. Possible spirit shapes: Eagle, Rattlesnake, Claw Strider, Fox, or Badger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T07:17:09-07:00","id":1301303,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to try an Ichneumon Hunter Totem Lunar, giving birth to Beastmen is so much easier when you can make someone else do all the hard work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11006-bowerbird","name":"Bowerbird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T07:38:36-07:00","id":1301306,"title":"","content":"So I found this picture of a panther-owl griffon and I am becoming obsessed about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not clear yet on the concept but probably a No-moon witch.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://eportfolios.macaulay.cuny.edu/hannarose/files/2016/03/Owl-Griffin.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Hana Rose is the name of the artist. <a href=\"https://eportfolios.macaulay.cuny.edu/hannarose/2016/03/12/owl-griffon/\" target=\"_blank\">https://eportfolios.macaulay.cuny.ed...2/owl-griffon/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 03-31-2019, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T04:50:25-07:00","id":1302165,"title":"","content":"I was just watching a show on PBS's youtube content on Eurypterids. And now I'm trying to think of a Lunar concept with a sea scorpion totem....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:25:54-07:00","id":1302197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1300697#post1300697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wicked old sorcerer who, reliving the moment that sent him down his dark path, finally did the right thing. Exalted, he has been returned to boyhood through something like the Blessed Transformation, and now he's out to <i>earn</i> this second chance while trying to be rid of the man he was.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a somewhat similar vein ... a tyrannical witch-queen who was coming to the end of the extended lifespan she gave herself with sorcery, and managed to botch the desperate working to give herself true immortality. She returned to the prime of her youth as she intended, but in mind as well as body.<br /> <br /> She wakes up in a circle of standing stones, miles from home and centuries in the future, newly exalted and confused as hell. Everyone she knew is dead. People in the area speak of the terrible sorceress who rules with an iron fist and treats with devils and goes by a name she recognises as one she used to use in childish games of make-believe when she was younger. She knows things without quite knowing how she knows them - how to split her palm into a hellish maw that sucks the moisture from her enemies and leaves them as desiccated husks, how to call forth demons from nightmare realms beyond imagining - but is haunted by disturbing visions of her former life. <br /> <br /> She believes her memory loss is a gift from Luna, a cleansing madness sent by the goddess of lunacy to scour away the deeper corruption of the spirit that overwhelmed her some unknown time ago. She's caught between wanting to find out what sent her down that path in the first place and being afraid to probe her own memory too deeply lest she lose herself again, but she can't escape the need to set right what she can and heal the damage she has done, which means she won't always have a choice but to plumb those depths. <br /> <br /> Oh, and she's definitely got a dread manse out there somewhere full of forbidden lore and sorcerous tomes and task-bound guard demons that don't recognise her anymore and magical traps she can't remember. Should be fun.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking rabbit totem, since they're vulnerable prey animals with a surprising amount of fight in them, symbolically associated with rebirth and madness (and of course, the moon). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:31:30-07:00","id":1302259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1302197#post1302197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a somewhat similar vein ... a tyrannical witch-queen who was coming to the end of the extended lifespan she gave herself with sorcery, and managed to botch the desperate working to give herself true immortality. She returned to the prime of her youth as she intended, but in mind as well as body.<br /> <br /> She wakes up in a circle of standing stones, miles from home and centuries in the future, newly exalted and confused as hell. Everyone she knew is dead. People in the area speak of the terrible sorceress who rules with an iron fist and treats with devils and goes by a name she recognises as one she used to use in childish games of make-believe when she was younger. She knows things without quite knowing how she knows them - how to split her palm into a hellish maw that sucks the moisture from her enemies and leaves them as desiccated husks, how to call forth demons from nightmare realms beyond imagining - but is haunted by disturbing visions of her former life.<br /> <br /> She believes her memory loss is a gift from Luna, a cleansing madness sent by the goddess of lunacy to scour away the deeper corruption of the spirit that overwhelmed her some unknown time ago. She's caught between wanting to find out what sent her down that path in the first place and being afraid to probe her own memory too deeply lest she lose herself again, but she can't escape the need to set right what she can and heal the damage she has done, which means she won't always have a choice but to plumb those depths.<br /> <br /> Oh, and she's definitely got a dread manse out there somewhere full of forbidden lore and sorcerous tomes and task-bound guard demons that don't recognise her anymore and magical traps she can't remember. Should be fun.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking rabbit totem, since they're vulnerable prey animals with a surprising amount of fight in them, symbolically associated with rebirth and madness (and of course, the moon).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is this Revan from KOTOR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T09:20:16-07:00","id":1302580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1302259#post1302259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is this Revan from KOTOR?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers, I guess, for the few people who don't know how the story of KOTOR goes by now.<br /> <br /> Not entirely. Revan had an entirely fictitious past implanted in their head and thus took much longer to catch on, whereas my time-lost sorceress accurately remembers her life up to a point and then has a ~300 year blank in which she somehow becomes an evil witch queen. Revan is also less of a fish out of water because their fake memories are constructed to make sense for the time and place, and the world is still familiar to them for the most part, whereas being centuries out of touch is a whole different experience. But in as much as they're both mind-screwed formerly evil protagonists on a redemption quest (if you're playing light-side Revan), sure, there's definite similarities. She's not intended to be an expy but I do like that story so I'm not above drawing inspiration from it (you've got me wondering who her Malak is, now). I like redemption arcs in general, if done well.<br /> <br /> I also like characters who are a bit of a mystery to themselves. I once played a character in a superhero game who was a total amnesiac and no longer felt connected to the identity of who she was before, even though she had scrapbooks and diaries and loving parents trying to remind her. I pointed the GM at the blank space in her backstory where she was missing for three days and gained her powers and said &quot;surprise me&quot;. I even left the possibility that she wasn't actually the original, but some kind of defective copy, on the table (this was actually her personal theory. It made her feel really guilty and alienated and drove a lot of her heroism). It was great. Her condition of course turned out to have been caused by the main plot so we got to unravel both at the same time and discover who/what she was as we discovered what was going on. It's something I recommend doing at least once if you have a GM you trust. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T12:13:49-07:00","id":1302613,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking right now of a big burly and jovial northern No Moon, with a narwaal horn sticking out of his face","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T12:36:13-07:00","id":1302615,"title":"","content":"so,will he be a jedi of the sea?<br /> <br /> ok as long as he stops Cthulhu from eating me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T21:48:58-07:00","id":1302739,"title":"","content":"I had a fun idea for a boisterous gorilla totem Full Moon based loosely on General Trayster from Venture Brothers who claimed all his hearts blood by wrestling everything using one of those charms that let you tweak how you take forms. Dunno if it'd work, but it would be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T10:21:34-07:00","id":1302858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288542-lunars-you-re-looking-forward-to-creating-with-the-new-book?p=1299630#post1299630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wary of any sentiments that would lean in the direction of &quot;there are good Dynasts and there are bad Dynasts, and the bad ones just happen to have more authority&quot;, or even flirt coyly with it from across the room.<br /> <br /> But not quite in the manner of expressing discontent with the monarchy by hunting slaves for sport.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these days much more thought goes into whether the books employ an example of something happening or reference a broad social trend.<br /> <br /> A recent example of this being done right is Amatha Kinslayer's relationship with her husband. It's not shocking that a male Dragon-Blooded would treat his mortal wife like a concubine, but I think if the notion of such a thing had been addressed in What Fire Harth Wrought then it would've overshadowed the potentially interesting status quo of the husband joining the wife's household.<br /> <br /> Conversely, while I didn\u2019t need her backstory to tell me that the Realm being matrilineal and matriarchal wouldn\u2019t protect women from domestic abuse or that Dragon-Blooded men could still wield considerable power over the opposite sex in the Realm\u2019s new framework, I\u2019m sure for some it\u2019s going to be a light bulb moment that brings life to a character concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-05-2019, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}